  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Goalkeeper – rushed shooter in two against two",
  "description": "Two against two towards one goal with a goalkeeper, in an area about 25 metres wide and 30 metres long. The coach stands at the far end with balls. The blue pair attacks for three minutes in a row, and the red pair defends. When red wins the ball they play it to the coach, who straight away plays a new ball in to blue.\n\nThe defenders are always close, so whoever gets free rarely has time to control the ball and aim. During some periods, goals only count from inside a cone line about ten metres from goal. That gives more breakaways with a defender on the attacker’s heels – go back to normal if play starts to feel unnatural.\n\nSwap attack and defence after three minutes and count goals per pair. With four pairs, two play and two rest. Variation: two goalkeepers, one per team, taking turns in goal. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "If the shooter has a defender behind them, come out fast and make the target smaller."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Read the touch – a long touch is your chance to take the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Stop and get set before the shot, even when you are on your way out."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "If you can’t get there, go down wide with your hands towards the ball and block."
    }
  ],
